# Headers for assets Cloudflare serves directly from the Workers Static Assets
# binding, WITHOUT invoking the Worker.
#
# This matters: the prerendered pages (/, /studio, /contact, /privacy, /terms,
# /404) are static files, so src/middleware.ts never runs for them. Without
# this file they would ship with none of the hardening headers. The dynamic
# routes (/creations, /api/*, /admin) are handled by the Worker and get the
# same set from the middleware — one set, two delivery paths, no gap.
#
# NOTE ON COMMENT SYNTAX: this file uses `#`, not C-style `/* */`. A leading
# `/*` is parsed as a PATH PATTERN, not a comment, which is why the previous
# version of this file produced 16 "invalid header rules" warnings per build and
# only applied its headers by accident.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is deliberately absent. Astro generates it per
# page, with that page's exact script hashes, and delivers it in a <meta> element
# on the HTML itself. A static header cannot know those hashes, and a second
# policy would intersect with the real one and block the site's own scripts.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), browsing-topics=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'

/admin*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Cache-Control: no-store

/api/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Cache-Control: no-store

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/og-default.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
